Base the default AWKPATH and AWKLIBPATH on where gawk.exe is installed.

DEFPATH and DEFLIBPATH are compiled in from the build prefix; conda does
not relocate paths inside binaries on Windows, so an installed gawk looked
for its awk library in the build directory.

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index d8f7750..85139b8 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -242,6 +242,11 @@ main(int argc, char **argv)
 
 	os_arg_fixup(&argc, &argv); /* emulate redirection, expand wildcards */
 
+#ifdef __MINGW32__
+	/* Before the options: -i and -l look up their files right away.  */
+	w32_relocate_default_paths();
+#endif
+
 	if (argc < 2)
 		usage(EXIT_FAILURE, stderr);
 
